rooms_desc ({"you enter the house and you notice that it is very expensively decorated.The floor is marble and there is a silk chinese area rug in the center.Hanging from the ceiling is an antique Tiffany's crystal chandeleir.","This is the display room for Dallion's classic automobilesHere you see a 300SL, an XK-E, a Lotus Super Seven, a Talbot Lagoa Type 57 SC, a Rolls 20/25 and Silver Cloud.  You also see Dallion's reveryday autos; a 1991 Lotus Espirit SE, and the new Bentley Turbo R.","This room is decorated in dark oak.  Shelves of books reach from floorto ceiling.  You wonder if Dallion has read them all.  you notice in thecorner a leather wing-back chair that looks broken in and comfy.You also notice Dallion's cat, Beamer, sitting in the chair and yourealize that if you try to sit there she'll kick your ass.","This room is decorated in pickled pine and hunter green.  The carpet is a deep shade of hunter green.  The bed is HUGE, and looks very comfortable.you notice Dallion's other cat, Duchess, on the bed.  you decide that youdon't want to mess with her either.","This is the garage in which Dallion restores his autos.  In the corneris a chassis for a Type 904 porsche.  On the rack is a restored Porsche 550 Spyder waiting for a new transmission.  In the corner of the shop is Dallion's McLaren F1 that he uses for the fun of out-runningthe police on saturday nights.","You enter a room with white walls and floor.  In the corner you see the latest model Cray computer.  In the center of the room is a table with sttel legs and a glass top.  On the table you see a phone a black split keyboard, a mouse, and a joystick.  In the ceiling you see mounted an SVGA projection monitor that is pointed at the wall that the desk faces. you figure that it must cast an image at least seventy inches (177.8 cm) wide.  In the walls on either side of the desk are mounted HUGE speakers.  you realize that they must be hooked up to the CRAY in the corner.  you feel that Dallion's soul is in this room and you start to understand that his life is empty except when the computer is on.","This is the room where Dallion displays the art he has bought.The artists are not necessarily, and may never be, famous.The art is not necessarily expensive.  This is art that Dallion likes;not some jerk from New York, LA, or San Francisco.  Dallion Doesn't carewhat is stylish, and you notice this.  You also notice that while Dallionis always increasing his collection it is ALWAYS tasteful.","This is the depression room.  It is empty except for a single chair in the center of the room.  The room is lit by a single light-bulbsuspended from the ceiling.  The walls, floor, and ceiling are paintedin dark swirls that show madness and pain.  This is where Dallion comes to think when he is disappointed in his life.  This is where Dallion has been spending much of his time.",0,0,})
rooms_short ({"This is the entrance to Dallion's house.","You have entered the display room.","This is the study.","This is the bedroom.","The garage.","This is the computer workroom.","This is the art display room.","The depression room.",0,0,})
